**How to implement.** The Launcher's footer opens Data locations (001 §O 'A footer link opens Data locations'; 001 §G; .spec-md §10.1: the Launcher's footer link opens Data locations). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588`): `launcherDataLocationsLink` (`"LauncherDataLocationsLink"`) with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow(locations, settings, opened, pickerFor)` (steps 88, 89, 154, 180): its footer, the bottom-docked row of the version line (`Program.fs:179-189`), gains on its left a link-styled `Button` reading `Data locations` (transparent background, no border, underlined text, font size 11) carrying `launcherDataLocationsLink` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, whose click opens `DataLocationsWindow(locations, ExplorerProxy.system)` (steps 183, 194) through `WindowLauncher.create` over that factory, `settings.selectWindowModality` and `BrowseOpen`, under `DataLocationsWindowKey`, so a second click brings the open window forward. The link is in every outcome's content and always enabled, a library that failed to open included, because the locations do not depend on the library (step 88). The `LauncherWindow` doc names the link in no more words; no other launcher control changes. (3) Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs`, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: the Data locations link opens one Data locations window listing the configured locations`: over `TestAppScope.testLocations`, raising `Click` on `launcherDataLocationsLink` as the file's launcher facts click opens exactly one `DataLocationsWindow`, whose kits row's `dataLocationPathText` reads the test kits folder's text, and a second click opens no other window; the window is closed at the end. `the Data locations link stays enabled when the library fails to open`: over `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr …)`, as step 88's fact builds the launcher, `launcherDataLocationsLink` is enabled while the four surface buttons are disabled. No fact presses Open folder through the launcher, because its explorer is the system's.

**Acceptance.** After the footer link lands, the Launcher MUST show `launcherDataLocationsLink`, enabled in every outcome, opening one Data locations window over the configured locations; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Data locations link opens one Data locations window listing the configured locations` and `the Data locations link stays enabled when the library fails to open`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
